sva.tooltip.details.buggy=A light ground vehicle for early trips and scouting.
sva.tooltip.vehicle.stats=Tier %s. Up to %s km/h, seats: %s, cargo: %s slots. Climbs one-block steps.
sva.tooltip.vehicle.energy=Uses %s EU/t at full speed (more with cargo), %s EU/t idling. A full charge lasts ~%s blocks.
sva.tooltip.vehicle.limits=Empty battery: limp mode (10%% speed). At 100%% heat the motor stalls until it cools to 50%%. Deep water can't be crossed.
sva.tooltip.howto.vehicle1=Right-click a block top: place. Right-click the vehicle: get in (only the owner drives, others ride as passengers). Shift: get out.
sva.tooltip.howto.vehicle2=W/S throttle and reverse, A/D steer, Space brake. Shift + right-click: cargo. Shift + right-click with a Silicon Age wrench: pick the vehicle up (charge and cargo are kept).
sva.tooltip.howto.vehicle3=Charges on a "Vehicle Charging Station". Repair for now: right-click with a steel ingot (+10%%), later in the Garage.
sva.tooltip.charger.summary=§7Input: §f%s§7, charges a vehicle at up to §f%s EU/t
sva.tooltip.charger.details=Charges a vehicle standing on the station or on the plates of its platform (up to 64 plates) from its buffer. Joins the Silicon Age or IC2 grid and takes up to %s (%s EU/t) - anything higher blows it up. Upgrades: overclocker, transformer, energy storage; modules: gas, repair, access.
sva.tooltip.howto.charger=Run a cable to it. Without plates the vehicle must touch its top; with plates - stand on the platform. Right-click: the station screen (platform, vehicle, upgrades, modules, settings). A comparator reads the vehicle's charge.

