key.sva.down=Descend (helicopter - collective down, plane - nose down; the sprint key works too)
sva.tooltip.vehicle.statsAir=Tier %s. Up to %s km/h, seats: %s, cargo: %s slots. Ceiling: Y 200.
sva.tooltip.details.heli=Takes off and lands anywhere: mountains, islands, rooftops. Hovers in place, flies forward and back, turns on the spot.
sva.tooltip.energy.heli=Uses %s EU/t hovering, %s EU/t flying forward (climbing costs more, descending less), %s EU/t on the ground. A full charge lasts ~%s blocks of flight.
sva.tooltip.vehicle.gas.heli=Helium cools the motor above 40%% heat: without it a long hover overheats the motor - and the helicopter goes into autorotation.
sva.tooltip.limits.heli=Out of charge, overheated, wrecked or with nobody at the controls in the air - §eautorotation§7: a slow spiral down and a landing; the hull loses at most 10%%, the people are unhurt. Jump out in the air and you fall as usual.
sva.tooltip.howto.heli2=Space - collective up (take off, climb), the Descend key (X) or sprint (Ctrl) - down, neither - hold the height. W/S - forward / back, A/D - turn. Shift+right-click - cargo.
sva.tooltip.howto.heli3=Pad: a Vehicle Charging Station with a 5x5 of plates ("H" plates mark it for helicopters). Helium: a cell / bucket or a Gas Column.
sva.tooltip.details.plane=Long trips for little: at cruise height (Y 100 and up) it uses 20% less. Needs speed - it can't take off from a standstill.
sva.tooltip.energy.plane=Uses up to %s EU/t on the take-off run and climbing, %s EU/t cruising (20%% less above Y 100), %s EU/t on the ground. A full charge lasts ~%s blocks.
sva.tooltip.vehicle.gas.plane=Helium cools the motor above 40%% heat: a long full-throttle climb without it overheats the motor.
sva.tooltip.limits.plane=Take-off run ~30 blocks (half on a Runway). Below 36 km/h in the air - §estall§7: the nose drops and it loses height. Without the motor - a 1:8 glide and a belly landing that wears the hull. It can't hover.
sva.tooltip.howto.plane2=W/S - throttle up / down (on the ground at zero throttle S brakes), A/D - banked turn, Space - pull up (on the ground: lift-off from 40 km/h), Descend (X) or sprint (Ctrl) - nose down, neither - hold the height. Shift+right-click - cargo.
sva.tooltip.howto.plane3=Take off: full throttle, run, Space. Land: descend, touch down (no faster than 6 m/s down), throttle to zero and S to brake; a runway brakes softly, hard braking on bare ground scuffs the hull.
sva.tooltip.runway.summary=§7Plane take-off run x0.5, soft braking
sva.tooltip.runway.lit=§eEdge lights - glow (light %s), seen at night
sva.tooltip.runway.details=A plane rolling on a runway speeds up twice as fast - ~15 blocks to lift-off instead of ~30 - and brakes softly, without hull wear. The centre line follows the look of whoever places the block.
sva.tooltip.howto.runway=Lay a strip 3 blocks wide and 20+ long, the edges with lights. Made on the Engineering Workbench: smooth stone x6, glowstone, redstone, steel ingot -> x8; lit: runway x4 + glowstone dust.
sva.msg.autorotation=§6The helicopter lost power - autorotation: a spiral down and a landing
sva.msg.glide=§6No thrust - gliding 1:8, find a place to land
